            <ArticleTitle>Post-anesthesia uncal herniation secondary to a previously unsuspected temporal glioma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>900-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 21-year-old male who sustained an uncal herniation and subsequent brain death following general anesthesia, for a minor orthopedic procedure, owing to the presence of a large, unsuspected temporal glioma. The possible factors responsible for the precipitation of this event are appraised.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
